codex
The paper’s decisive point is now clear: its proof is constructive in the algorithmic sense. Procedure 1 reduces a tree-factor packing to perfect matchings in bipartite “super-edges,” and arbitrary perfect matchings combine into a tree factor. That rules out a Track A claim for the paper’s random/pseudorandom distribution; I’m testing whether a legitimate Track B family can preserve those native blow-up objects while offering a short structural route that is much smaller than matching search.
exec
