A closer reading of the packing requirement exposed an improvement: distinct affine maps with different slopes intersect, so they would not give edge-disjoint factors. I’m tightening the construction to parallel affine matchings—one common slope and distinct intercepts per lane. The requested witness is now an exact decomposition into edge-disjoint P4-factors covering every graph edge, matching the paper’s packing object rather than merely finding one factor.
