The concurrent worker has stopped, so I audited its replacement rather than discarding it. Its \(F_q^3\) construction is stronger than my scalar draft: shuffled vertex IDs hide two affine perfect matchings, while coordinatewise neighbor sums recover each matrix in 280 operations; the generic affine-basis search measured tens of thousands of field operations per instance. Seven gates pass. I found one genuine G2 bug—a “swap” corruption sometimes swapped equal values and remained valid—and am fixing that before hardening.
