+"""Affine-encoded tree factors in the blow-ups of arXiv:1304.2429.
+
+Section 3 of Bal--Frieze--Krivelevich--Loh turns a fixed tree into a
+multipartite blow-up and observes that one perfect matching on each
+super-edge composes to a tree factor.  This module uses T=P4.  In each
+coordinate lane the same bipartite graph is placed on all three
+super-edges; that graph is constructed as a union of affine perfect
+matchings over a prime field.  The answer is one affine map per lane.
+
+Generation is inverse: the affine matchings are sampled before the graph is
+assembled, and a sampled member of every lane is retained as the witness.
+No matching or affine-map search is performed by make_instance().
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
