Implemented a provisional Track B generator based on Section 3’s composition of super-edge perfect matchings into a \(P_3\)-factor in the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.2429).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1304_2429.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/gen_1304_2429.py)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/README.md)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/selftest_report.json)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Exactly 121 valid certificates among \(1.3428\times10^{20}\) candidates.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four tool-free attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, as expected for Track B.
- Answer: 146 characters, 24 elements.
- Intended compact route: 280 operations.

The result is not yet shippable: all bare, hinted, and placebo oracle calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently no attempts were scored, G9 remains false, and `all_passed` is honestly false. No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure block, not a family rejection.

After restoring OpenRouter quota, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1304_2429.py
```

Then rerun the hinted and placebo arms in separate scratch directories and update `G9_ORACLE_RESULTS`. Redundant scratch directories were moved to trash after their transcripts were preserved.
