codex
The full gate run caught a real construction leak: 256 random affine-basis restarts solved 2 of 8 seeds, so G6 correctly failed. I’m not weakening the attack. I’ll add a paper-native alignment witness: the certificate will include a translation shared by the two matching families. The matrix still certifies the full packing, while the shared translation identifies one aligned `P3` factor. At degree 20 this cuts random-restart success by another factor of 20 and leaves a 270-operation compact route.
apply patch
