-two matching certificates themselves; there is no graph-to-CSP reduction.
+Section 1 fixes the exact factor definition: copies need not be induced, are
+vertex-disjoint, and cover every vertex. Section 3 defines a blow-up of a
+fixed tree. In the proof of Theorem 1, immediately after Lemma 3.4, arbitrary
+perfect matchings on the t-1 super-edges are united into a T-factor. This
+module uses exactly those native objects with T=P3. Each super-edge is a
+union of d edge-disjoint affine perfect matchings; pairing the two matching
+families gives d edge-disjoint P3-factors covering every displayed edge. The
+answer also identifies a translation shared by the two families, hence one
+aligned P3-factor in that packing.
 
-STEP 0 rules out Track A. The same Section 3 proof explicitly obtains the
