 ## Caveats
 
-This is a native tree-blow-up/factor problem, but the finite-field coordinates
-and affine answer compression are generator structure, not a distribution
-studied by the paper. It exercises the matching-composition step of Section 3,
-not the full approximate packing theorem and not `G_{n,p}` pseudorandomness.
+The graph and factor packing are native paper objects, but finite-field affine
+coordinates are generator structure, not the random or pseudo-random
+distribution analyzed by the paper. The task exercises the matching-composition
+step of Section 3, not the asymptotic hypotheses of Theorems 1–3.
 
-The exact G5 density is relative to the declared prior of two uniformly random
-affine bijections. It is not a density among arbitrary explicit perfect
-matchings, nor a Bayesian estimate for a solver exploiting adjacency. The
-attack panel tests degree/frequency outliers, lexicographic basis choices, 256
-random basis-image restarts, and the identity-matrix ansatz. It does not test
-all algebraic-recovery methods, SAT/ILP encodings, or learned recognition. In
-fact the neighbor-sum decoder deliberately solves every instance efficiently;
-that is the Track B compact route. A graph matcher also finds an explicit
-`P3`-factor quickly, although the required output is the affine coefficient
-compression rather than a long edge list. Most importantly, no model-hardness
-claim is justified until the quota failure is cleared and all three transcript
-arms contain scored attempts.
+The G4 probability is relative to uniform invertible matrices and uniform
+offsets—the bounded language a reader gets from the statement. It is not a
+density among arbitrary explicit perfect matchings and does not predict a
+structure-aware model. Marginally, planted and decoy translations are sampled
+the same way; the answer is distinguished relationally by membership in both
+translation sets.
+
+The panel tested target-frequency outliers, lexicographic basis choices, 256
+random basis-image restarts, and the identity ansatz. It did not test every
+SAT/ILP encoding, learned affine recovery, or every algebraic moment method.
+Generic bipartite matching can find a long explicit factor packing but does not
+directly produce the required compressed affine certificate. `canonical_key`
+uses a joint within- and cross-set projective-direction invariant because full
+simultaneous affine-set isomorphism is not known to be cheap; it can theoretically
+collide on non-isomorphic instances even though all 20 unrelated audit keys were
+distinct. Most importantly, the current files establish correctness and local
+attack resistance only—not LLM hardness—until the account-level quota blocker
+is cleared and a scored bare transcript exists.
