The construction is now fixed: a native packing problem using the paper’s basic \(K_2\)-factor (perfect matching). Each graph is the union of many edge-disjoint affine perfect matchings over a prime field; the answer is a short symbolic list of affine maps, not thousands of edges. All factors are sampled from the same distribution, so there is no statistically special “planted” layer. The Track B contrast is exact affine-map enumeration versus a neighbor-sum invariant that exposes the shared slope.
