+The answer is a symbolic packing, not a list of its (kp) edges. `verify` expands every polynomial over all (p) residues, checks every edge, proves that each right side is covered once, and checks edge-disjointness. It accepts every valid list of affine factors and never reads `inst["answer"]`.
 
-## Why Track B is the honest claim
+## Why this is Track B
 
-Track A would be false. Section 1 identifies the `K2` case with ordinary
-perfect matching, and Section 3 obtains tree factors from bipartite perfect
-matchings. Lemma 3.4 handles regular pseudo-random pairs; Lemma 4.1 handles
-random bipartite pairs. Theorem 2 assumes `epsilon^4 n p >> log(n)^2`, while
-Section 5 notes the opposite obstruction: below roughly `log(n)/n`, isolated
-vertices prevent even one factor.
