codex
Implemented and verified a Track B generator based on the paper’s \(K_2\)-factor packing objects ([arXiv:1304.2429](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.2429)).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/gen_1304_2429.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [Harness metadata](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1304.2429/.meta.json)

Results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `hard`, \(p=509\), 80 affine matching layers, 6 requested factors.
- Exact structure-aware answer density: \(2.52\times10^{-8}\); sampled guesses: 0/200,000.
- Five adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: mean 256,030 exact operations; compact invariant route: 186 operations.
- Bare oracle ladder: easy 3/3 solved, medium 2/3 solved, hard 0/3 solved—final verdict `hardened`.
- G9: hinted 1/3, placebo 1/3, so hinted-minus-placebo is 0.
- Answer size: 53 characters, 12 atomic coefficients.
